-- CONTROL for #1275. This harness grades a control on its EXIT CODE ONLY and a
-- control must exit 0, so it cannot be the "correctly rejects" cell (exit 1).
--
-- It exercises the SAME call shape through the SAME re-exporter and the SAME
-- import form as main.mdk, with `Blob` implementing `MB` -- the interface the
-- occurrence actually names. A valid program that must print 7. If it breaks,
-- module re-export / selective-import obligation recording broke, not #1275.
--
-- ⚠️ It deliberately does NOT import ifacea, which is what keeps bys.mdk (the
-- bystander) out of THIS entry's module graph. That is not tidying: with the
-- ifacea import present, this very program -- impl `MB`, occurrence meaning
-- `MB.mth` -- is REJECTED with `No impl of MA for Blob` (measured; see
-- claim.txt). That mirror is the same defect with the sign flipped, and it
-- cannot serve as a control precisely because it exits 1.
import mid.{MB, mth}

public export data Blob = Blob

export impl MB Blob where
  mth b = 7

main = println (mth Blob)
